WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.200
You're stung by a jellyfish.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.380
What's your first course of action?

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.820
Maybe home remedies pop into your mind

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.520
peeing on the sting site,

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.240
applying ice or using baking soda.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.080
If tentacles are sticking to your skin, you probably feel

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.360
like you want to scrape them off.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.660
But none of these treatments work, and some will make things worse.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.220
And if you're stung by a box jellyfish, that could make

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.260
the difference between life and death.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.820
We're in an area where there's very

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.680
little tolerance for mistakes,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.280
and things that make things worse are a real tragedy

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.340
in our mind.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.960
That's Angel Yanagihara, a researcher at the University of Hawaii at Manoa

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.560
who has been studying jellyfish venom for two decades.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.920
Box jellyfish, members of the Cubozoa class,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.400
live in tropical and temperate waters around the world.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.920
They're common in the Pacific, near the coast of the

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.160
Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand, Malaysia and Australia.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.789
They inject venom into your skin by firing

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:04.860
microscopic hypodermic needles at speeds

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.180
of more than 60 kilometres an hour.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.640
The venom is a chemical cocktail that at

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.360
high doses can cause cardiac arrest in

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.940
less than five minutes.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.240
Yanagihara has developed products to counter the sting,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.260
a spray containing vinegar and urea

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.200
and a cream containing copper gluconate.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.528
The spray , so it stops the cells from firing

00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:30.200
the tentacle from firing all this venom.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.220
It doesn't stop the venom that's already in the body.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.340
The cream on the other hand, does that.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.180
Yanagihara stresses that some home remedies

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.820
also work. Simple vinegar can stop unfired venom cells

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.100
as well. and heat can block venom already injected.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.970
Not everybody agrees however, one scientist

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.180
says vinegar can actually make things worse.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.280
All jellyfish venom scientists agree

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.860
that more research is needed on how the venom works,

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.340
and what can be done to stop.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.900
In just the months of June and July itself

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.600
there were at least three kids,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.440
I guess you can call them, who died from

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.280
box jellyfish in the Philippines itself.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.040
It might just seem like a minor part of

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.520
the first-aid compendium and what does

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.390
it matter if you say put ice on it or

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.240
put heat on it or put either on it.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.980
If one takes a global perspective, then it's

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.620
pretty clear pretty rapidly why that matters.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.120
Another question needs more research as well,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.600
how many people get stung by jellyfish

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.880
and how many die?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.340
There are no official statistics, and Yanagihara thinks the

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.591
problem is more serious than people realize.

00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:40.980
When I went to these rural health offices

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.200
and I would ask the group how many people had been

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.840
stung by a box jellyfish, a good third in a lot of

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.530
these places would raise their hands.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.740
Unfortunately in the Philippines, most of

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.920
these deaths aren't recorded, aren't ever reported

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.060
forward. They're considered environmental accidents, and

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.460
so they're basically lost to us.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.260
To get a better handle on the problem, Yanagihara's

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.320
team is surveying health workers and coastal

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.300
communities in the Philippines.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.420
They're also educating people about the risk of jellyfish

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.660
stings, and conducting research on the jellyfish population.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.580
So we see our role there in a three-part way.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.700
One is the public health piece, which is getting the data.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.920
One is the public education piece, which is about

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.580
prevention and understanding, and then the third piece

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.680
is just the field ecology.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.180
Better understanding jellyfish ecology might

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.700
help prevent injury, because people could

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:38.513
be warned about when to avoid the water.

00:03:38.513 --> 00:03:41.049
The solution could be as simple as just

00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:44.080
making people realize that this is

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.600
this can kill this is when it comes,

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.780
don't really go into the sea at this at this point of the year.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.880
By showing that jellyfish are a serious public health

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.660
problem, Yanagihara hopes that research funders

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.200
will pay more attention.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.139
If jellyfish stings are underreported, basically they

00:04:02.139 --> 00:04:04.800
don't meet even the most minor threshold

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.500
for any asset allocation.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.240
Professional scientists need to be really even more

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:17.780
engaged in the public sphere, and in cases in which

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.840
There's real emotional pain and suffering,

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.820
if scientists stay in the ivory tower,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.280
The general populace doesn't feel connected with scientists.

